WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.667 --> 00:00:02.708
And I'm sympathetic
to your struggle, truly.

00:00:03.833 --> 00:00:04.667
But there's a protocol

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:06.833
to visiting a patient
like Victor.

00:00:06.917 --> 00:00:08.208
You have to put in
a request.

00:00:08.833 --> 00:00:10.750
And then you have to undergo
a screening process,

00:00:10.833 --> 00:00:11.667
at which point

00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:13.125
the board
will make a decision.

00:00:16.208 --> 00:00:17.417
I can see
you're disappointed.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:19.833
But I'm more than happy

00:00:19.917 --> 00:00:21.167
to give you a tour
of our facility?

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:23.083
Perhaps, you can even speak
to some patients

00:00:23.167 --> 00:00:24.917
in our low-security wing.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.833
And we'd,
we would love that.

00:00:28.417 --> 00:00:33.250
It's just that our thesis
is due next month.

00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:35.000
Then you're out of time.

00:00:35.083 --> 00:00:36.125
Who's fault is that?

00:00:36.208 --> 00:00:38.125
Ours. Absolutely.

00:00:38.208 --> 00:00:41.167
-And I do apologise--
-Don't apologise, Ruth.

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:42.292
Screw that!

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:43.750
The fact of the matter is

00:00:43.833 --> 00:00:45.583
we did put in a request
months ago and were denied.

00:00:45.667 --> 00:00:48.250
And then we reapplied
and were denied again.

00:00:48.333 --> 00:00:50.500
And coming here,
was our last-ditch effort

00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:52.500
to save our thesis,
and I really,

00:00:52.583 --> 00:00:54.292
I can't breathe
in this thing.

00:00:54.375 --> 00:00:56.500
Well, Rose, maybe
you'd like to go outside

00:00:56.583 --> 00:00:57.417
and get some air?

00:00:57.500 --> 00:00:58.833
Maybe I should, Ruth.

00:00:59.458 --> 00:01:01.458
Because I'm starting
to think this whole thing

00:01:01.542 --> 00:01:03.167
is a colossal mistake.

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:05.000
I'm breaking out in a rash,

00:01:05.083 --> 00:01:07.583
my boobs hurt,
and I'll tell you the truth,

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:08.833
Anthony,
may I call you Anthony?

00:01:08.917 --> 00:01:10.667
These aren't actually
my clothes.

00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:11.708
I borrowed them

00:01:11.792 --> 00:01:13.625
because I wanted you
to take us seriously,

00:01:13.708 --> 00:01:15.750
because nobody takes girls
seriously in this field.

00:01:15.833 --> 00:01:18.417
They just don't.
We don't look the part,

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:20.667
or whatever,
but can I tell you a story?

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:23.208
1978, I was at summer camp,

00:01:23.292 --> 00:01:24.583
and my counsellor, Drew,

00:01:24.667 --> 00:01:26.583
told me
and everyone in cabin C

00:01:26.667 --> 00:01:29.167
the true story of
the Victor Creel massacre.

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:32.167
And little Petey McHugh,
you know Petey, right, Ruth?

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:34.042
-Of course.
-Yeah.

00:01:34.125 --> 00:01:36.292
Little Petey McHugh
started sobbing

00:01:36.375 --> 00:01:37.542
right there on the spot.

00:01:37.625 --> 00:01:40.250
Full on hyperventilating
and all the other campers,

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:41.458
they couldn't sleep
for weeks.

00:01:41.542 --> 00:01:43.750
And I couldn't sleep either,
but not 'cause I was scared,

00:01:43.833 --> 00:01:45.708
because I was obsessed
with the question:

00:01:45.792 --> 00:01:47.208
what would drive
a human being

00:01:47.292 --> 00:01:49.708
to commit
such unimaginable acts.

00:01:49.792 --> 00:01:50.833
Other kids,

00:01:50.917 --> 00:01:52.250
they wanted to be
astronauts,

00:01:52.333 --> 00:01:53.542
basketball players,
rockstars,

00:01:53.625 --> 00:01:54.750
but I wanted to be you.

00:01:54.833 --> 00:01:56.542
I wanted to be you,

00:01:56.625 --> 00:01:59.792
so forgive me if I'll now
try anything in my power,

00:01:59.875 --> 00:02:02.292
including wearing
this ridiculous outfit,

00:02:02.375 --> 00:02:04.125
if I might get the chance
to speak to the man

00:02:04.208 --> 00:02:05.375
that ignited my passion

00:02:05.458 --> 00:02:07.500
and learn a little bit more
about how his twisted,

00:02:07.583 --> 00:02:08.792
but let's face it,

00:02:08.875 --> 00:02:11.250
totally fascinating mind,
works.

00:02:11.333 --> 00:02:14.375
So, yes, we don't have
the "official" paperwork,

00:02:14.458 --> 00:02:17.208
but don't tell me
that crybaby Petey McHugh

00:02:17.292 --> 00:02:19.000
wouldn't have gotten
an audience with Victor

00:02:19.083 --> 00:02:21.042
in a matter of moments
if he'd asked politely

00:02:21.125 --> 00:02:23.208
'cause you and I both know
that he would!

00:02:24.333 --> 00:02:27.458
So… ten minutes with Victor.

00:02:28.667 --> 00:02:30.042
Is all I ask.

00:02:34.375 --> 00:02:36.000
I'm back in thirty.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.333
We did it!

